The MIT terms above cover the source code in this repository.

They do not override the licences of the third-party data and images that are
committed alongside it, each of which keeps its own terms. Those are listed in
full under "Credits and licences" in README.md. Two carry conditions worth
naming here, because they travel with the files rather than with the code:

- public/data/stars.json is derived from the HYG Database v4.1 and is therefore
  CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistributing that file, or a database derived from it,
  carries the same share-alike condition.
- public/data/skymodel.json is fitted to Globe at Night observations. The
  coefficients are this project's own work; the observations behind them belong
  to the Globe at Night programme and its contributors.

Every spacecraft photograph under public/bodies/ is public domain, verified at
fetch time by scripts/fetch-bodies.mjs, which refuses to ship anything else.
